# Removes the part 2 rooms' items outright, instead of replacing them with a
# harmless placeholder (176). The original "SOME ITEMS MAY REMOVE OTHERS"
# fear was a false alarm: it was caused by listing the removeitem() calls in
# ASCENDING index order, so each removal shifted the still-pending targets'
# indices out from under the next call. Removing in DESCENDING order (as
# below) avoids that entirely -- verified empirically this session: the
# resulting entity list and floordata item-references match exactly what was
# intended, byte for byte, with nothing else touched.
#
# This is now the FULL list from the "Items to be removed" comment above (88
# items) -- the earlier version only implemented 19 of those 88 (apparently
# abandoned mid-work), leaving 69 items still sitting, fully visible, in the
# supposedly-emptied part-2 rooms. Found by cross-checking every entity's
# room against the part-2-room list and comparing against what was actually
