# Fixes rooms 14 and 44 being 34 clicks tall, 3 clicks over the PSX room
# format's 31-click vertex-height limit (tr3pcpsx would otherwise silently
# truncate these vertices' Y-value, corrupting the geometry -- this is what
# the FindingTheLost's "temporary fix" (resizeroom above) was trying and
# failing to work around). The affected vertices all belong to a purely
# decorative "abyss" floor sitting well below the room's real
# (FloorData-defined) walkable floor, so raising them by 768 units (3
# clicks) is invisible to gameplay/collision and only makes the decorative
# drop 3 clicks shallower. Y-parameter is height-above-yBottom (trmod
# convention), computed as yBottom - (original_Y - 768). Verified with a
# clean tr3pcpsx conversion (zero Y-value warnings).
./trmod tr3pc undersea.tr2 "replacevertex(14,6,,,1280)" "replacevertex(14,8,,,1024)" "replacevertex(14,10,,,1280)" "replacevertex(14,37,,,1280)" "replacevertex(14,43,,,1280)" "replacevertex(14,79,,,768)" "replacevertex(14,81,,,768)"
./trmod tr3pc undersea.tr2 "replacevertex(44,76,,,1280)" "replacevertex(44,79,,,1280)" "replacevertex(44,81,,,1280)" "replacevertex(44,86,,,768)" "replacevertex(44,89,,,768)" "replacevertex(44,91,,,768)" "replacevertex(44,96,,,768)" "replacevertex(44,99,,,768)" "replacevertex(44,101,,,768)"

